course: dictionary
lesson: 7698
title: Who provides?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A provider is a person or company that supplies something people need. «An email is sent to your email provider's server and passed to the other person's server.» The words around provider tell you it is a company that runs the email service for you, so it is the one that gives you email.
explain: Provider can also mean a person who earns money to support a family. Read the clue in «the main provider»: main means most important, so the main provider is the person who brings in the money the family relies on.
explain: In formal writing, provider can mean any person or group that gives a service, like a childcare provider. Check your meaning by swapping it in. Does "a childcare service that gives childcare" still make sense? If it does, you have it right.
fact: A provider is a person or company that supplies something people need, such as electricity, internet or health care.
fact: «Internet provider», «service provider» and «health care provider» are all useful phrases to remember.
fact: «The main provider» means the person who earns money to support a family.
fact: In RE, Christians believe God is the provider of all good things.
fact: Context clue: if a sentence is about bills, the internet, a family or a service, provider probably means someone who supplies what people need.
exercise: «An email is sent to your email provider's server and passed to the other person's server.» What is an email provider? | A type of computer mouse | *A company or service that gives people email | A person who delivers letters by post
exercise: Ella says, «Dad is the main provider.» What does provider mean here? | A shop assistant at the supermarket | The person who cooks the dinner every night | *The person who earns money to support the family
exercise: Which word means a person or company that supplies something people need? | *provider | puzzle | furniture | holiday
test: «The internet provider fixed the line within an hour.» What is the internet provider? | Someone who sells old computers | A kind of router sold in shops | *The company that supplies the internet | A website about games
test: Which is an example of a service provider? | A sunny day | A pencil case | *A childcare provider | A school bag
exam: What does provider mean in the phrase «health care provider»? | A medicine that tastes nice | A doctor's waiting room | *A person or group that gives health care | A bag for carrying medicine
